SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of enabling human life on Mars.
&gt;
&gt; NEW GRADUATE PROPULSION ENGINEER, RAPTOR
&gt;
Join the forefront of space exploration at SpaceX as a member of the Raptor team - the worlds most advanced rocket engine powering Starship&#x27;s journey in making humanity multiplanetary. If you&#x27;re eager to tackle real-world challenges in propulsion systems, from mechanical design and analysis to manufacturing and testing - this is your opportunity to help build the worlds most powerful rocket engine with an emphasis on efficiency and reusability. Bring your innovative mindset and strong fundamentals in engineering principles to drive the boundaries of what&#x27;s possible.
&gt;
RESPONSIBILITIES:
&gt;
Expect a dynamic role doing what you&#x27;re best at. Our team is building high performance flight hardware, a high-volume rocket engine production line, and a propulsion system that can rapidly and reliably power our rockets. Whatever your skill set, you&#x27;ll be aligned to the part of the program you&#x27;re most effectively able to contribute to.
&gt;
Own the design and development of next generation rocket engines, test stands, and production lines.
&gt;
Perform hand calculations and FEA to develop, assess, and optimize designs.
&gt;
Rapidly iterate on manufacturing processes and development testing in a fast-paced environment.
&gt;
Collaborate with interdisciplinary teams to ensure hardware integrates with all Raptor systems and supports necessary mission operations.
&gt;
Own large business outcomes and experience a rate of personal and professional growth that is unmatched literally anywhere else.
&gt;
Get a front row seat to witness an impossible idea manifest in real life. The next few years will be incredibly dynamic as we transition from the challenge of building hardware to…

About the role
&gt;
Muon is seeking a part-time Co-Op Harness Designer to join our electrical engineering team, intended for students in the surrounding area. Working under the mentorship of current harness designers, you will specify connectors, crimps, wire types, and harness build instructions. You will also need to be flexible and incorporate feedback from the AIT team to improve designs for spacecraft integration and testing. This role involves working simultaneously across multiple missions and projects while partnering with various engineers, designers, and technicians.
&gt;
This is a hybrid role that requires regular on-site collaboration with our engineering team.
&gt;
Responsibilities
&gt;
Create harness drawings, BOMs and maintain system diagrams
&gt;
Specify connector and crimp part numbers in accordance with system design
&gt;
Gather feedback from AIT, EE and Mechanical for initial designs and improvements
&gt;
Work with electrical engineering to ensure compliance with signal integrity, grounding, and shielding requirements
&gt;
Release documentation into PLM with ECO/DCO
&gt;
Answer vendor questions on harness builds and feedback quality issues
&gt;
As required assist in house technicians with harness builds and questions
&gt;
Qualifications
&gt;
Attention to detail, strong reading comprehension and a desire for ownership
&gt;
Some experience creating harness drawings or electrical schematics in any software (school projects, clubs, or personal builds count)
&gt;
Basic familiarity with, or willingness to learn, how harnesses are built from scratch.
&gt;
Excited to work in a fast-paced environment with new challenges each week
&gt;
Nice-to-have Skills
&gt;
While not a daily requirement, hands-on intuition helps inform strip lengths, crimper settings, splicing techniques, heatshrink selection, and torque values.
&gt;
Familiarity with NASA-STD-8739.4 and IPC-A-620
&gt;
Basic scripting skills in Python, Bash, etc.
&gt;
History with using electrical test equipment, such as power supplies and electric…

At Affirm, we exist for the moments that matter-giving people a clear, predictable way to pay over time, with no hidden fees, no surprises, and no tradeoffs on what matters most.
&gt;
&gt; Our team owns the refund experience for Affirm customers. We build the customer-facing features, backend services and data foundations that make refunds clear, fast and reliable. Refunds touch a large share of our customers, so the work has a direct, visible impact on their trust in Affirm. We&#x27;re a growing team with a full roadmap, which means we can invest consistently in this area.
&gt;
We&#x27;re collaborative and ownership-minded. Engineers own their work from design through on-call, raise risks early, and share what they learn. We care about clear written communication and constructive code review, and we work closely with partner teams across the company.
What You&#x27;ll Do
&gt;
With the support of your team, you will work on tasks that contribute to the team&#x27;s projects and goals.
&gt;
You will work collaboratively and proactively with your team and stakeholders, bringing them along for your work and helping to create visibility and dialog regarding the risks and trade-offs related to your work.
&gt;
You will strike the right balance of speed and quality in your work, ensuring that we hit our business goals while protecting our systems from downtime.
&gt;
You will contribute to a sense of community on your team by engaging in growth and development activities.
&gt;
What We Look For
&gt;
You have previous work or internship experience shipping web apps using declarative UI frameworks like React or Vue.
&gt;
You have previous work or internship designing, developing and launching APIs at scale using languages like Python or Kotlin.
&gt;
You have mastered taking a simple problem or business scenario into a solution that interacts with multiple software components, and executing on it by writing clear, easily understood, well tested and extensible code.
&gt;
You are comfortable navigating a large code base, debugging…

Who we are
&gt;
Samsara (NYSE: IOT) is the pioneer of the Connected OperationsTM Cloud, which is a platform that enables organizations that depend on physical operations to harness Internet of Things (IoT) data to develop actionable insights and improve their operations. At Samsara, we are helping improve the safety, efficiency and sustainability of the physical operations that power our global economy. Representing more than 40% of global GDP, these industries are the infrastructure of our planet, including agriculture, construction, field services, transportation, and manufacturing - and we are excited to help digitally transform their operations at scale.
&gt;
Working at Samsara means you&#x27;ll help define the future of physical operations and be on a team that&#x27;s shaping an exciting array of product solutions, including Video-Based Safety, Vehicle Telematics, Apps and Driver Workflows, and Equipment Monitoring. As part of a recently public company, you&#x27;ll have the autonomy and support to make an impact as we build for the long term.
&gt;
&gt; About the role:
&gt;
We are looking for a self-starting, motivated, and experienced Collections Specialist to support the small business globally. The Collection Analyst oversees the accounts receivable efforts of a global portfolio of monthly receivables and acts as the conduit between the sales team, the customer, and corporate. This opportunity requires a candidate with a high volume accounts-centric mindset, high attention to detail, excellent problem-solving abilities, and an enthusiastic attitude. Candidates must have the ability to juggle multiple tasks and priorities, thrive in a highly driven environment, enjoy learning new skills, procedures, and systems, and have an overall desire to contribute to company growth. This position plays an essential role in minimizing our financial loss by implementing receivable and collection procedures that reduce the amount of delinquency encountered and reports to our Sr. Manager, Order to…

Please note that while we accept applications for our internship position starting in the fall, we will not begin actively contacting candidates for interviews until/after November 2026.
&gt;
Our Summer Internship Opportunity:
&gt;
This internship program will provide you with the opportunity to apply the economic concepts you&#x27;re learning in the classroom in a professional services setting. It will also help you to improve your research and data analysis skills as well as learn to manage and prioritize tasks. You will work side by side with internationally recognized experts in financial economics, corporate finance, energy, competition, and regulatory economics.
&gt;
Securities Intern Role
&gt;
As a Research Analyst intern at The Brattle Group, you will be integral to our project teams, collaborating with senior consultants and experts. Your responsibilities will include:
&gt;
Quantitative Models and Solutions: You&#x27;ll build financial, economic, and operational models using Excel (e.g. valuation models, estimating cost of capital). You may also build models and create innovative data-based solutions for clients using programming languages, for example in Python, R, SAS, Stata, and VBA.
&gt;
Qualitative Research and Literature Review: You&#x27;ll conduct comprehensive research, including financial statements, market analysis, literature reviews, document examination, and writing memos to provide insights and support expert reports.
&gt;
Supporting Expert Witnesses: You&#x27;ll assist in preparing expert reports and presentations, helping our experts present complex economic and financial concepts clearly in legal and regulatory contexts.
&gt;
Collaborating with Team Members: Effective communication and teamwork are critical. You&#x27;ll work closely with colleagues at all levels, contributing to the development of robust and innovative solutions for our clients.
&gt;
Typical Assignments Might Include:
&gt;
Accounting: Assessing a company&#x27;s internal controls to identify manipulation and any improper revenue…

Overview:
&gt;
Astera Labs Inc. is seeking an experienced and self-driven Hardware Lab Engineer to join our dynamic team in developing world class connectivity products for AI infrastructure.
&gt;
Job Description
&gt;
This is an entry-level role in Post-Si Electrical Validation working with low-level electrical signals in the lab to validate the performance of high-speed ASICs on PCIe and DDR interfaces. Our team works closely with firmware, system validation, quality, and product engineers to support silicon bring-up, characterization, and debug activities through hands-on lab execution. The ideal candidate will have a deep understanding of analog and digital circuits, signal integrity, python automation, and the ability to work on complex, open-ended tasks with minimal oversight.
&gt;
Key Responsibilities
&gt;
Setup and maintain test environments for silicon validation and characterization. Configure and update hardware, software, firmware, and applications.
&gt;
Conduct hands-on testing of silicon devices including PCIe Gen5/6/7, CXL, DDR, and other high-speed interfaces
&gt;
Use high-speed oscilloscopes and Bit-Error-Rate-Testers (BERTs) to validate Tx and Rx compliance to spec.
&gt;
Manage logistics and communications with external vendors
&gt;
Develop, document, and maintain lab procedures
&gt;
Required Qualifications
&gt;
Bachelor&#x27;s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or related field
&gt;
0-2 years of hands-on experience in lab environments supporting silicon validation or hardware development
&gt;
Knowledge of analog/mixed-signal circuit testing and debugging techniques
&gt;
Strong programming skills in Python for test automation
&gt;
Familiarity with Linux operating systems and command-line tools
&gt;
Strong written and verbal communication skills and ability to track multiple details in parallel.
&gt;
Preferred Qualifications
&gt;
Master&#x27;s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or related field
&gt;
Experience with post-silicon validation of ASICs, SoCs, or Retimer/PHY…

&gt;
At Accenture Federal Services, nothing matters more than helping the US federal government make the nation stronger and safer and life better for people. Our 13,000+ people are united in a shared purpose to pursue the limitless potential of technology and ingenuity for clients across defense, national security, public safety, civilian, and military health organizations.
&gt;
&gt;
Join Accenture Federal Services, a technology company within global Accenture. Recognized as a Glassdoor Top 100 Best Place to Work, we offer a collaborative and caring community where you feel like you belong and are empowered to grow, learn and thrive through hands-on experience, certifications, industry training and more.
&gt;
&gt;
Join us to drive positive, lasting change that moves missions and the government forward!
&gt;
&gt;
&gt;
&gt; Job Description
&gt;
Supports ServiceNow development activities for the ServiceNow project under the guidance of senior development staff. Applies foundational ServiceNow platform knowledge to assist with configuration, basic scripting, and application customization. Develops proficiency in ServiceNow development tools, best practices, and federal requirements while building hands on platform development experience.
&gt;
Key Responsibilities
&gt;
Performs basic ServiceNow configurations including forms, lists, fields, and UI customizations
&gt;
Develops simple scripts including Client Scripts, UI Policies, and basic Business Rules under guidance
&gt;
Assists with data imports using Import Sets and Transform Maps
&gt;
Supports Flow Designer workflow development and maintenance
&gt;
Creates reports and dashboards using ServiceNow reporting tools
&gt;
Assists with ServiceNow integration testing and troubleshooting
&gt;
Documents configuration changes, technical specifications, and user guides
&gt;
Supports update set management and deployment activities
&gt;
Participates in Agile ceremonies including daily standups and sprint reviews
&gt;
Learns ServiceNow platform capabilities, development tools, and…

Who we are
Pronto AI is a global leader in commercializing autonomous vehicle (AV) technology, deploying Autonomous Haulage Systems (AHS) that automate operations in mines, quarries, and construction sites worldwide. While much of the industry remains in R&amp;D, we deliver real, production-ready autonomy that is already operating in the field.
We are on a mission to make mining operations safer, smarter, and more efficient through cutting-edge technology, and we are building toward becoming the world&#x27;s first profitable AV technology company.
&gt;
&gt;
About the role
&gt;
We are looking for a driven and curious Industrial Engineering (or related field) intern to join our operations team. This is a hands-on, rotational internship. You will work across multiple departments, tackle real problems, and be expected to deliver real results. If you are the type of person who seeks out the hard work others avoid, you will thrive here.
&gt;
&gt;
What you&#x27;ll do
&gt;
This is a rotational internship. Over the course of the programme, you may work across areas including
&gt;
Quality assurance and non-conformance management
&gt;
Inventory control and warehouse operations
&gt;
Procurement and supplier management
&gt;
Supply chain operations
&gt;
Product and Manufacturing Planning
&gt;
Internal process documentation and improvement
&gt;
Specific responsibilities may include
&gt;
Mapping, documenting, and improving operational processes using frameworks such as SIPOC and RACI
&gt;
Supporting the implementation and management of internal tools and platforms (task management, internal communications, project tracking)
&gt;
Identifying and flagging inefficiencies, bottlenecks, and non-conformances
&gt;
Assisting in structuring departments or workflows that need reorganization
&gt;
Collaborating cross-functionally with engineering, supply chain, finance, and leadership teams
&gt;
&gt;
What we&#x27;re looking for
&gt;
Currently enrolled in a Bachelor&#x27;s program in Industrial Engineering, Systems Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, Operations Management,…

Who we are
Pronto AI is a global leader in commercializing autonomous vehicle (AV) technology, deploying Autonomous Haulage Systems (AHS) that automate operations in mines, quarries, and construction sites worldwide. While much of the industry remains in R&amp;D, we deliver real, production-ready autonomy that is already operating in the field.
We are on a mission to make mining operations safer, smarter, and more efficient through cutting-edge technology, and we are building toward becoming the world&#x27;s first profitable AV technology company.
&gt;
&gt;
About the role
&gt;
We are looking for a hands-on, detail-oriented Mechanical Engineering intern to join our growing hardware team in Brazil. This is a dynamic role combining technical documentation, prototype development, and field installation work. You will be essential to scaling our hardware systems globally, working directly with our US-based mechanical engineering team while managing both office and field responsibilities. If you are the type of person who wants to understand how things actually work and isn&#x27;t afraid to get your hands dirty, this is the role for you.
&gt;
&gt;
What you&#x27;ll do
&gt;
Over the course of this internship, you will gain exposure across multiple technical areas:
&gt;
Producing detailed engineering drawings, assembly instructions, Bills of Materials (BOMs), and technical documentation
&gt;
Designing, building, and assembling both prototype and production units
&gt;
Performing test fits and validating prototype designs
&gt;
Installing hardware systems on large-scale equipment (including mining trucks over 100 tons)
&gt;
Collaborating with US-based mechanical and electrical engineering teams on design and deployment support
&gt;
Traveling to client sites for initial installations and system development (up to 30% of the time)
&gt;
Working with local Brazilian suppliers to manufacture custom components (sheet metal, machined parts, etc.)
&gt;
Specific responsibilities may include
&gt;
Creating CAD models and engineering drawings with…

This position is open exclusively to current Northeastern University Co-Op students.
Work Period: January 2027 to June 2027. This is a full - time, 40 hours per week position with 5 days in office.
About Fathem
&gt;
Fathem is pioneering Visual IntelligenceTM to transform how scientists see, understand, and design biology. At the core of this vision is molecular vision at scale-the ability to directly observe molecular structure with the speed, throughput, and accessibility required to make it the central technology for drug creation. To achieve this, Fathem is innovating at the interface of cryo-electron microscopy, AI, enabling hardware, and automation.
About Flagship Pioneering
&gt;
Fathem was founded by Flagship Pioneering&#x27;s venture creation engine that invents and builds platform companies, each with the potential for multiple products that transform human health or sustainability. Since its launch in 2000, Flagship has originated and fostered more than 100 scientific ventures, resulting in more than $90 billion in aggregate value. Many of the company&#x27;s Flagship has founded have addressed humanity&#x27;s most urgent challenges: vaccinating billions of people against COVID-19, curing intractable diseases, improving human health, preempting illness, and feeding the world by improving the resiliency and sustainability of agriculture. Flagship has been recognized twice on FORTUNE&#x27;s &quot;Change the World&quot; list, an annual ranking of companies that have made a positive social and environmental impact through activities that are part of their core business strategies and has been twice named to Fast Company&#x27;s annual list of the World&#x27;s Most Innovative Companies. Learn more about Flagship at www.flagshippioneering.com .
&gt;
Flagship Pioneering Co-Op Program
&gt;
Welcome to Flagship Pioneering Co-Op Program for the cohort dreaming big and taking courageous leaps. You&#x27;ll join fellow peers across our ecosystem of companies and learning firsthand how we build first-in-category companies.…

&gt;
At Woolpert, you&#x27;ll do work that matters.
&gt;
As a leading global architecture, engineering, and geospatial firm, we help clients solve complex challenges that shape communities, strengthen critical infrastructure, advance technology, and improve the world around us. Here, you&#x27;ll collaborate across disciplines, tackle meaningful projects, and build a career defined by growth, opportunity, and impact.
&gt;
&gt;
&gt;
Position Overview
&gt;
Seeking a new career challenge? Then Woolpert is seeking you! Woolpert is hiring a Survey Intern to join our Survey and Geospatial team for the 2027 internship program . This full-time internship provides students with the opportunity to gain hands-on experience supporting field and office surveying operations while working alongside experienced survey professionals on a variety of infrastructure, transportation, aviation, utility, and geospatial projects.
&gt;
As a Survey Intern, you will assist with collecting, processing, and analyzing survey data that supports engineering design, construction, mapping, asset management, and community development initiatives. You may contribute to boundary and topographic surveys, control surveys, mobile and terrestrial laser scanning, UAV support operations, GIS data collection, transportation asset inventories, and other geospatial projects that directly impact the communities where we live and work.
&gt;
This intern will be a full-time position for both field and office operations out of multiple locations with opportunities to travel. Woolpert does not provide relocation assistance for interns.
&gt;
Woolpert is unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Applicants must already possess authorization to work in the country where this position is located.
&gt;
What You Will Do
&gt;
Work as an integral member of a survey field crew and project team.
&gt;
Assist licensed surveyors, survey technicians, and geospatial professionals with field data collection activities.
&gt;
Operate and learn advanced surveying…

Persons in these roles are expected to work from our offices in Seattle. On-site requirements vary based on position and team. If you have questions about on-site work arrangements for this role, please ask your recruiter.
&gt;
*Compensation dependent on current degree enrollment.
Research Intern, Undergrad: $94,320 (Annually)
Research Intern, Masters: $106,110 (Annually)
Research Intern, PhD: $140,000 (Annually)
&gt;
Who You Are:
&gt;
Are you interested in researching cutting-edge developments in AI applied to climate modeling? Do you have a passion for applying technology to do good in the world? If so, an Ai2 research internship in the Climate Modeling team may be the perfect opportunity. We will be offering 12-week internships during summer 2027. We will review applications and schedule virtual interviews for top candidates in January-February 2027.
&gt;
Ai2 Research Internship Information:
&gt;
Duration : 12 weeks
&gt;
Start Date : Flexible
&gt;
Candidates : A PhD student with a strong research background
&gt;
Please apply by January 4, 2027, at 11:00pm Pacific Time to be considered for our Spring/Summer 2027 internships.
&gt;
Who We Are:
&gt;
Ai2&#x27;s Climate Modeling team (Ai2CM) has developed ACE, the world&#x27;s leading AI-based global atmosphere emulator for climate applications. ACE can be trained to replicate weather variability and climate change at 100 km horizontal resolution using historical observations or outputs from any physics-based climate model. It runs hundreds of times faster on a single GPU than such a model running on a supercomputer. For climate-planning applications, we have implemented diffusion-based super-resolution for downscaling ACE simulations to kilometer-scale local detail. We also recently began a collaboration with Google Research to advance NeuralGCM, a hybrid AI-physics model, for climate projection applications.
&gt;
Your Next Challenge:
&gt;
At Ai2, you will be working with world-class AI researchers and software engineers. We perform team-based, ambitious…

ABOUT ROCKET LAB
&gt;
Rocket Lab is the end-to-end space company building rockets, spacecraft, and critical subsystems that keep the world connected, protected, expand humanity&#x27;s reach to the Moon, Mars, and beyond. We move fast, build real hardware for meaningful missions, and make the impossible routine. Come shape the future with us.
&gt;
&gt; SPACE SYSTEMS
&gt;
At Rocket Lab, we&#x27;re not just launching rockets - we&#x27;re building the future of space. Our Space Systems team builds everything from complete spacecraft, precision payloads to the components and subsystems that allow them to thrive in space, like solar panels, flight software, star trackers, optical systems, separation systems, radios, and more.
&gt;
Our Space Systems team has enabled more than 1,700 missions, ranging from interplanetary exploration, in-space manufacturing to national security and defense initiatives. The team has built spacecraft, payloads, and components for missions to the Moon and Mars, working with partners including NASA, the Space Development Agency, and the U.S. Space Force. Whether it&#x27;s a single high-performance spacecraft, constellation, or the vertically integrated components that help them get to space - our world class Space Systems team is empowering some of the boldest and most ambitious space missions.
&gt;
RADAR RF DESIGN ENGINEER I
&gt;
Based at Rocket Lab&#x27;s global headquarters in Long Beach, CA, we are looking for a Radar RF Design Engineer I who will support the development of radar and RF systems including SAR (Synthetic Aperture Radar) and space-based radar applications. You will work alongside experienced radar engineers to develop radar subsystems, conduct analysis and simulation, and support hands-on testing and integration activities. The successful candidate will have foundational knowledge of radar systems, RF engineering principles, and basic understanding of orbital mechanics and spacecraft systems, and will thrive in a fast-paced, dynamic environment.
&gt;
WHAT YOU&#x27;LL GET TO…

Who we are
Pronto AI is a global leader in commercializing autonomous vehicle (AV) technology, deploying Autonomous Haulage Systems (AHS) that automate operations in mines, quarries, and construction sites worldwide. While much of the industry remains in R&amp;D, we deliver real, production-ready autonomy that is already operating in the field.
We are on a mission to make mining operations safer, smarter, and more efficient through cutting-edge technology, and we are building toward becoming the world&#x27;s first profitable AV technology company.
&gt;
&gt;
About the Role
&gt;
We are looking for a curious and practical Robotics intern to support our Autonomous Hauling System (AHS) team. You will work directly with real fleet operations, combining embedded systems, sensors, telemetry, navigation, log analysis, and field debugging. This is a learn-by-doing role where you&#x27;ll gain hands-on experience across the full stack of autonomous vehicle systems. If you want to understand why machines behave the way they do and aren&#x27;t afraid to get into the technical weeds, this is the internship for you.
&gt;
&gt;
What you&#x27;ll do
&gt;
Over the course of this internship, you will gain exposure across autonomous system operations and diagnostics:
&gt;
Support routine autonomous system testing following defined checklists, procedures, and protocols
&gt;
Provide first-level technical support for actuators, electronics, sensors, telemetry, embedded computers, and navigation systems
&gt;
Assist in initial diagnostics of autonomy kit failures by correlating reported symptoms, logs, vehicle state, and operational conditions
&gt;
Collect, organize, and tabulate fleet performance data to support engineering team analysis
&gt;
Analyze field logs and evidence to identify patterns, root cause hypotheses, and next investigation steps
&gt;
Document and categorize tickets, incidents, non-conformances, and technical findings with full traceability
&gt;
Support installation, replacement, inspection, and validation routines for electronic and…

Airbnb was born in 2007 when two hosts welcomed three guests to their San Francisco home, and has since grown to over 5 million hosts who have welcomed over 2 billion guest arrivals in almost every country across the globe. Every day, hosts offer unique stays and experiences that make it possible for guests to connect with communities in a more authentic way.
&gt;
&gt; The community you will join:
&gt;
Airbnb is seeking a Partnerships Enablement Intern to join the Partnerships &amp; Business Development team for France and Benelux for a 6-month internship.
&gt;
The goal of our Partnerships &amp; Business Development team is to build from the ground up partnerships and alliances to support Airbnb&#x27;s business and growth. They are responsible for deal making and partners management from A to Z. Starting with sourcing stakeholders who could become partners tomorrow, to implementing the partnerships per se, all the while working to ensure successful, long-lasting relationships with all the stakeholders.
&gt;
&gt;
The difference you will make:
&gt;
You&#x27;ll be joining the team at a particularly exciting moment : we&#x27;re building our local strategy from the ground up, about to launch a major partnership, and driving an innovative new project. You&#x27;ll get 360° exposure to business development, with a strong focus on activation: event execution, stakeholder alignment, and impact tracking. It&#x27;s an opportunity to contribute to a high-impact launch, learn what great outcomes look like, and build the foundation to engage future partners with confidence.
&gt;
You can expect to:
&gt;
Partner with your mentor - Business Development Lead for France and Benelux - to oversee activation plans for ongoing partnerships
&gt;
Contribute to event coordination: this involves planning, stakeholder management (both internally and externally), D-day activation, and last but not least, after-action review to guarantee solid measurement practices, feedback collection and suggest improvements
&gt;
Participate in mapping out potential new…

Credit Summer Intern
&gt;
SUMMARY
&gt;
The 10-week Summer Internship Program is designed to provide an introduction to the alternative investment industry, specifically alternative credit strategies such as credit hedge funds and private credit. Interns receive real-world experience that will foster professional development while complementing their studies. Internships in the Credit department are geared towards rising seniors pursuing a career in the investment management industry.
&gt;
The intern will be based out of our Chicago office.
&gt;
CREDIT INTERN
&gt;
The Credit Team&#x27;s primary focus is to identify, underwrite, and monitor investments within investment managers and related opportunities on a global basis using both primary and secondary channels. The team covers a variety of alternative credit strategies such as long/short, distressed, structured, direct lending, specialty finance, and asset-backed. The credit summer intern will have exposure to the entire credit investment process from research to portfolio construction/monitoring and is expected to participate in projects and responsibilities as a full member of the team.
&gt;
RESPONSIBILITIES
&gt;
The individual will be involved in the following critical activities:
&gt;
Perform qualitative and quantitative analysis of existing and potential investments in alternative credit managers across both liquid (i.e., hedge fund) and illiquid (i.e., private debt) strategies.
&gt;
Track, analyze, and interpret trends in specific strategies and the related capital markets.
&gt;
Assess new investment strategies and monitor current conditions within existing strategies utilized by the firm.
&gt;
Prepare internal and external market and investment commentary on a monthly basis.
&gt;
Communicate manager and strategy-related issues to the Investments group, Investment Committee, and investors.
&gt;
Provide market, strategy, and manager insights to the broad Investment team.
&gt;
