We&#x27;re seeking a curious, analytical intern who brings a fresh perspective and is eager to help the Financial Planning &amp; Analysis team identify ways to improve. As a Financial Planning &amp; Analysis Intern at MongoDB, you&#x27;ll build relationships across the business and serve as a trusted partner to the Product &amp; Technology Finance team. You&#x27;ll develop a strong understanding of business drivers and how financial plans support MongoDB&#x27;s broader objectives.
&gt;
In this role, you&#x27;ll collaborate with stakeholders on budgeting, headcount planning, and resource optimization, while building and maintaining financial and operating models. You&#x27;ll also help improve how we input and manage forecasts in our financial systems, and conduct ad hoc analyses to inform operating strategies, resource allocation, and investment decisions for product initiatives.
&gt;
What we are looking for in you:
&gt;
In the process of receiving a Bachelor&#x27;s or Master&#x27;s degree in Finance, Economics, Math or a related field
&gt;
Foundational experience using data and spreadsheets to support decision-making, with curiosity about a career in financial planning and analysis.
&gt;
Uses sound judgment when working with incomplete data, making and clearly explaining reasonable assumptions while knowing when to pause and seek guidance.
&gt;
Ability to balance accuracy with efficiency, knowing when to prioritize each.
&gt;
Proficient in Microsoft Excel, Word, and PowerPoint and Google Sheets, Docs, and Slides
&gt;
Strong written and verbal communication and ability to collaborate effectively via Slack and other tools
&gt;
Have a minimum of one quarter/semester remaining in university studies after the internship concludes. Graduation date in Fall 2027 or Spring 2028
&gt;
Must be authorized to work in the United States.
&gt;
